# The assessment of WORK-LEDGER-001 against this build. The requirement identifier is this
# file's stem and appears nowhere inside it, because a second place to spell the identity is
# a second place for it to be wrong — the rule OD-SPEC-007 chose for a record registration,
# and CHK-003.assessment states for this registry.
#
# WORK-LEDGER-001 requires an item be addressable as an individual artifact with stable id,
# title, state, priority, rationale, territory, dependencies, blockers, claim lease,
# completion condition, verification predicate, and recorded completion evidence.
# `LedgerItem` carries every element of that list except `priority`, so the divergence is
# exactly one element wide. OD-LEDGER-017 is the record: it corrects OD-TRACE-001's count of
# the statement's elements, establishes that the requirement binds this build rather than
# being read out of scope, and defers `priority` on a stated ground — the corpus wants it as
# the first of three ranking keys and the other two are already derivable from `depends_on`
# and `territory`, so a bare integer would satisfy the letter while buying the key that ages
# worst. The record also names what makes the deferral wrong, which is what makes this a
# Diverges rather than a shrug.
#
# Two sites, because one would not decay. `LedgerItem` is the type the requirement is about
# and it will not vanish; `priority` occurs in this file only inside that type's doc comment,
# where OD-LEDGER-017 put the absent element so the verdict is readable at the type and not
# only in the record. Deleting that sentence is the change this entry must not survive.
#
# Not recomputed from the corpus at check time. OD-TRACE-001 records why: CI has no corpus,
# so a guard that read one would be green by being unable to look.
verdict: Diverges
record: OD-LEDGER-017
site: crates/substrate/nomos-ledger/src/item.rs#LedgerItem
site: crates/substrate/nomos-ledger/src/item.rs#priority
